<v Noah Labhart>Let's flip the script a little bit.

186
00:15:25.600 --> 00:15:29.460
<v Noah Labhart>Tell me about a mistake you made and how you and your team responded to it.

187
00:15:30.440 --> 00:15:37.460
<v Luca Rossi>So I think at the beginning, I was very afraid of publishing new articles and content.

188
00:15:37.960 --> 00:15:40.380
<v Luca Rossi>I'm a perfectionist by nature.

189
00:15:40.380 --> 00:15:48.140
<v Luca Rossi>so I tended to obsess a lot on over details, you know, of good writing on the articles.

190
00:15:48.420 --> 00:15:53.180
<v Luca Rossi>And I was really anxious, you know, before publishing a new piece.

191
00:15:53.400 --> 00:15:57.180
<v Luca Rossi>Every week in the beginning it was not even every week, it was every two weeks.

192
00:15:57.960 --> 00:16:03.680
<v Luca Rossi>I figured out how to cure it, I think, by forcing myself to publish more frequently.

193
00:16:04.560 --> 00:16:06.780
<v Luca Rossi>It's counterintuitive if you think about it.

194
00:16:06.780 --> 00:16:13.960
<v Luca Rossi>I mean, that if you are a perfectionist, the cure for it is to get more output, you know, to produce more things.

195
00:16:14.600 --> 00:16:27.180
<v Luca Rossi>But it works because when you have to create a lot of stuff in little time and you have a commitment, a public commitment to do that, you don't have time or energy to work through the details.

196
00:16:27.320 --> 00:16:30.340
<v Luca Rossi>And you eventually understand that they don't matter.

197
00:16:30.680 --> 00:16:33.840
<v Luca Rossi>I mean, at least they don't matter as much as you think they do.

198
00:16:33.840 --> 00:16:39.180
<v Luca Rossi>This is also something that I'm proud of, that I'm now comfortable in writing things online.

199
00:16:39.540 --> 00:16:42.780
<v Luca Rossi>And I tell this from the side of being an introvert.

200
00:16:43.000 --> 00:16:51.560
<v Luca Rossi>And so I feel that by writing every week and by becoming more comfortable about that, I've also grown as a person, as a human being in a way.

201
00:16:51.760 --> 00:16:53.360
<v Luca Rossi>But at the beginning, it was hard.

202
00:16:53.360 --> 00:17:06.000
<v Luca Rossi>So a mistake that I made is definitely to stumble too much on some things that I didn't feel like it would be worth publishing and then instead became some of the biggest successes of the newsletter, for example.

